.\" Man page for atlas status command
.\" Updated: July 2026
.TH STATUS 1 "July 2026" "atlas 0.13.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
atlas\-status \- project status management
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B atlas status
[\fIproject\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B atlas status
views or updates the .STATUS file for a project. The .STATUS file is a
YAML-format file tracking project state, progress, next actions, and
milestones.
.PP
When called without arguments, shows the status of the current directory's
project.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-set\fR \fIstatus\fR
Set project status: active, paused, blocked, archived, complete.
.TP
\fB\-\-progress\fR \fIpercent\fR
Set progress percentage (0\-100).
.TP
\fB\-\-focus\fR \fItext\fR
Set current focus area.
.TP
\fB\-\-next\fR \fIaction\fR
Set next action.
.TP
\fB\-\-complete\fR
Mark current next action as done.
.TP
\fB\-\-then\fR \fIaction\fR
After completing, add this as next action.
.TP
\fB\-\-increment\fR \fIamount\fR
Increment progress by amount.
.TP
\fB\-\-create\fR
Create .STATUS file if missing.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output as JSON.
.SH .STATUS FORMAT
The .STATUS file uses YAML format with these fields:
.PP
.RS
.nf
---
project: my-project
version: 1.0.0
status: active
last_session: 2026-07-11
branch: dev
type: node-package
priority: 1
progress: 75
next:
  - "Implement feature X"
  - "Write tests"
milestones:
  - "MVP released"
---
.fi
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
Show status of current project:
.RS
.nf
atlas status
.fi
.RE
.PP
Show status of specific project:
.RS
.nf
atlas status atlas
.fi
.RE
.PP
Set status to active:
.RS
.nf
atlas status \-\-set active
.fi
.RE
.PP
Update progress:
.RS
.nf
atlas status \-\-progress 80
.fi
.RE
.PP
Set next action:
.RS
.nf
atlas status \-\-next "Release v0.14.0"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Create .STATUS if missing:
.RS
.nf
atlas status \-\-create
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .STATUS
Per\-project status file (YAML format).
